i errors after v5.1.0 deploy \u2014 rolled back to v5.0.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "payments-api", "summary": "This morning's deploy of payments-api v5.1.0 left the service unhealthy, with an 18% error rate in us-east, us-west and eu-west. It was rolled back in all production regions to v5.0.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. Still to do: confirm error rates recover and find the root cause in v5.1.0.", "idempotency_key": "payments-api-v5.1.0-rollback-sev2", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_016NrWVPwdZAuxCvRtz9Fz6j", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-api", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled payments-api back to v5.0.0 and opened a SEV2 incident. The service is healthy again.\n\n- **Which service:** There's no service called \"payments,\" so I checked a few likely names. Only **payments-api** exists, and it was unhealthy on v5.1.0 (this morning's deploy) with an 18% error rate in us-east, us-west and eu-west.\n- **Rollback:** I rolled it back in all three regions to **v5.0.0**, its most recent release that was healthy in production. No approval was needed because that version has been healthy in production before. It's now healthy with a 0.2% error rate.\n- **Incident:** I opened **INC-0001 (SEV2)** for payments-api, which paged on-call. It describes the bad deploy and the rollback, and says the root cause in v5.1.0 still needs to be found.\n\nI only checked the names I could guess, so if another payments service (a worker, for example) was also in this morning's deploy, I haven't looked at it. Tell me its name and I'll check it.", "type": "text"}]}]}